Build QNX shared libraries with an soname.

support/shobj-conf has no case for QNX (nto-qnx*), so it reports shared
objects as unsupported and the libraries come out without DT_SONAME:
programs linked against them record libreadline.so -- the -dev symlink --
and fail to start where only the run-time package is installed. Add a case
with the Linux rules (lib<name>.so.<major> as the soname), minus the rpath
and minus the second -soname the Linux case puts in SHOBJ_LDFLAGS.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/support/shobj-conf
+++ b/support/shobj-conf
@@ -132,6 +132,20 @@
 	SHLIB_LIBVERSION='$(SHLIB_LIBSUFF).$(SHLIB_MAJOR)$(SHLIB_MINOR)'
 	;;
 
+# QNX Neutrino: as Linux, without the rpath (the libraries go where the
+# target's loader already looks, or LD_LIBRARY_PATH says).
+nto*)
+	SHOBJ_CFLAGS=-fPIC
+	SHOBJ_LD='${CC}'
+	# No -soname here: SHLIB_XLDFLAGS gives the library's. A second one naming
+	# the output file itself makes qcc stop with "input file ... is the same
+	# as output file".
+	SHOBJ_LDFLAGS='-shared'
+
+	SHLIB_XLDFLAGS='-Wl,-soname,`basename $@ $(SHLIB_MINOR)`'
+	SHLIB_LIBVERSION='$(SHLIB_LIBSUFF).$(SHLIB_MAJOR)$(SHLIB_MINOR)'
+	;;
+
 # Darwin/MacOS X
 darwin*)
 	# Common definitions for all darwin/mac os x versions
